      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You’re right—there is no point in rebuilding the same person. That person is gone, and mourning them is real. But the shame you carry? That’s just proof you still care enough to be hurt by it. The foundation’s gone, but you’re still here, breathing through the weight—that’s not nothing. Maybe you don’t rebuild what was lost; maybe you just let the ashes teach you what you refuse to become.",
